WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.400 --> 01:34.940
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.200 --> 01:37.789
[Episode 41]

4
01:47.560 --> 01:48.620
Is that enough ice?

5
01:49.430 --> 01:50.490
Is that enough ice?

6
01:51.640 --> 01:52.970
If not, I'll go get more.

7
01:55.860 --> 01:56.740
Here.

8
02:41.780 --> 02:42.180
Enlai!

9
02:42.180 --> 02:43.320
He's awake! He's awake!

10
02:43.320 --> 02:44.500
Enlai, you're awake!

11
02:44.500 --> 02:45.829
He's awake! He's awake!

12
02:46.020 --> 02:47.680
-Vice Chairman Zhou! -Enlai!

13
02:48.170 --> 02:48.670
Comrade Enlai!

14
02:48.670 --> 02:49.329
He's awake!

15
02:49.430 --> 02:50.110
Enlai!

16
02:51.870 --> 02:53.180
Vice Chairman Zhou!

17
02:54.550 --> 02:55.550
Comrade Wang Bin,

18
02:55.620 --> 02:56.300
Comrade Enlai is awake.

19
02:56.300 --> 02:57.329
Does this mean he's in the clear?

20
02:57.329 --> 02:59.079
The pus and blood have been drained.

21
02:59.079 --> 03:00.180
Thank God we got it out.

22
03:00.180 --> 03:02.430
Otherwise, even God couldn't have saved him.

23
03:02.430 --> 03:03.180
Enlai,

24
03:04.420 --> 03:06.880
you really owe Chen Geng a massive thank you.

25
03:06.900 --> 03:09.390
He ran dozens of miles on a bad leg,

26
03:09.580 --> 03:10.340
all the way up to the mountain peak,

27
03:10.340 --> 03:13.110
just to get that ice to cool your fever.

28
03:13.190 --> 03:15.990
That's the only reason the infection slowed down.

29
03:19.730 --> 03:21.100
Vice Chairman Zhou,

30
03:21.670 --> 03:24.270
you've got guardian angels watching over you.

31
03:26.110 --> 03:27.550
As for these two legs of mine...

32
03:27.550 --> 03:29.950
they saved Chiang Kai-shek back in the day,

33
03:30.110 --> 03:33.180
but bringing back this ice to cure you today.

34
03:34.430 --> 03:36.360
I'd say that wipes the slate clean.

35
03:41.990 --> 03:42.790
The troops...

36
03:44.270 --> 03:48.150
when do the troops move out?

37
03:48.550 --> 03:50.610
He's asking when the troops move out.

38
03:51.550 --> 03:52.410
Comrade Enlai,

39
03:52.750 --> 03:53.950
we head out tomorrow.

40
03:54.230 --> 03:55.500
The Central Committee has already decided.

41
03:55.500 --> 03:58.620
You and Comrade Jiaxiang, along with the other wounded,

42
03:58.620 --> 04:02.500
will travel with Peng Dehuai's 3rd Red Army.

43
04:03.180 --> 04:05.180
Just focus on resting and recovering.

44
04:05.180 --> 04:07.020
Don't worry about anything else.

45
04:07.020 --> 04:08.680
Don't you worry about a thing.

46
04:15.500 --> 04:16.390
Chen Geng...

47
04:20.500 --> 04:21.470
don't cry.

48
04:23.260 --> 04:24.020
Don't cry.

49
04:27.380 --> 04:34.300
Was it dangerous on the way back?

50
04:34.320 --> 04:35.560
Not at all.

51
04:36.260 --> 04:38.550
Good thing you and Chairman Mao

52
04:38.790 --> 04:40.450
managed to get a message to me.

53
04:41.030 --> 04:42.630
The second I got your letter,

54
04:42.790 --> 04:45.030
I rushed straight back from Zhuokeji.

55
04:45.380 --> 04:46.940
Otherwise, I'd be a dead man.

56
04:46.940 --> 04:47.870
What happened?

57
04:48.110 --> 04:49.230
Back in Heishui,

58
04:49.500 --> 04:52.590
Zhang Guotao kept beating around the bush,

59
04:52.920 --> 04:55.520
asking me about the differences

60
04:55.550 --> 04:56.940
between the 1st and 4th Red Armies.

61
04:56.940 --> 04:58.620
He was just fishing for something.

62
04:58.620 --> 05:00.110
So I just gave it to him straight.

63
05:00.110 --> 05:00.910
I told him

64
05:00.940 --> 05:03.870
some of the guys in the 4th Army

65
05:03.990 --> 05:04.870
have discipline issues,

66
05:04.870 --> 05:06.670
and zero sense of organization.

67
05:07.050 --> 05:08.510
He held a grudge over that.

68
05:08.820 --> 05:10.870
He teamed up with the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Committee

69
05:10.870 --> 05:11.940
to frame me.

70
05:12.870 --> 05:14.180
They were going to execute me.

71
05:14.180 --> 05:15.250
Thank God Comrade Deng Fa

72
05:15.250 --> 05:17.380
got word to us just in time.

73
05:17.990 --> 05:19.300
That Zhang Guotao...

74
05:22.700 --> 05:23.430
Enlai!

75
05:23.670 --> 05:24.790
Comrade Enlai!

76
05:25.220 --> 05:25.830
Enlai!

77
05:26.060 --> 05:26.870
Enlai!

78
05:26.940 --> 05:27.720
Vice Chairman Zhou!

79
05:27.720 --> 05:28.580
Comrade Enlai!

80
05:28.590 --> 05:29.620
You little punk,

81
05:29.700 --> 05:31.670
think before you speak from now on!

82
05:31.790 --> 05:34.190
What do you mean "he's not going to make it"?

83
05:36.300 --> 05:37.430
I was just scared!

84
05:41.350 --> 05:42.950
Don't be scared.

85
05:43.760 --> 05:44.740
It's okay. It's okay.

86
05:44.740 --> 05:45.870
Come on, get in here.

87
05:45.990 --> 05:47.920
Look. Comrade Enlai is awake.

88
05:48.380 --> 05:48.970
See?

89
05:50.940 --> 05:52.970
Comrade Enlai is awake!

90
05:54.290 --> 05:55.140
Jinbiao...

91
06:10.760 --> 06:12.240
The sun's gone down.

92
06:12.590 --> 06:13.500
I...

93
06:13.720 --> 06:15.520
This is cold too.

94
06:16.080 --> 06:17.340
The ice wasn't enough.

95
06:17.870 --> 06:19.110
Can we use this?

96
06:27.910 --> 06:28.990
Stop crying.

97
06:29.760 --> 06:30.720
We're all here.

98
06:32.230 --> 06:32.990
Stop crying.

99
06:33.850 --> 06:34.650
It's alright.

100
06:47.150 --> 06:49.560
In late August 1935,

101
06:50.030 --> 06:52.470
the Right Route Army split into two columns.

102
06:52.470 --> 06:54.940
Three regiments from the right flank vanguard,

103
06:54.940 --> 06:56.940
led by Ye Jianying and Cheng Shicai,

104
06:57.470 --> 07:00.150
entered the grasslands through Dongya and Lazishan

105
07:00.150 --> 07:02.670
on August 18th, 1935.

106
07:03.430 --> 07:07.230
The main forces of the 30th and 4th Red Armies followed close behind.

107
07:07.700 --> 07:11.620
On the left flank, with the 4th Regiment of the 1st Red Army leading the charge,

108
07:11.620 --> 07:15.430
troops marched from Mao'ergai through Qudingqiao into the marshlands.

109
07:15.430 --> 07:17.030
After August 22nd,

110
07:17.380 --> 07:19.360
the Central Committee and its directly affiliated units,

111
07:19.360 --> 07:22.180
along with the 3rd Red Army, set out from here one after another.

112
07:22.180 --> 07:25.060
Thus began the most extraordinary and grueling chapter

113
07:25.060 --> 07:28.460
of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army's Long March.

114
07:29.810 --> 07:31.820
[Huang Kaixiang, Commander of the 4th Red Regiment]

115
07:33.880 --> 07:35.630
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Red Regiment]

116
07:39.870 --> 07:40.820
Head north.

117
07:42.159 --> 07:43.760
This is our only way through.

118
07:44.350 --> 07:45.140
Understood.

119
07:47.990 --> 07:48.820
Got it.

120
07:58.060 --> 07:59.230
Listen up, comrades!

121
07:59.230 --> 08:01.090
Watch out for the deep sinkholes!

122
08:01.740 --> 08:02.500
Move out!

123
08:02.520 --> 08:03.520
Right!

124
08:03.820 --> 08:04.870
Let's move!

125
08:05.470 --> 08:06.500
Move out!

126
08:07.750 --> 08:09.070
I knew it.

127
08:10.300 --> 08:12.160
What did I just say at the meeting?

128
08:12.490 --> 08:13.950
No rushing blindly ahead.

129
08:14.180 --> 08:15.140
No wandering off.

130
08:15.140 --> 08:15.700
Yes, sir!

131
08:15.910 --> 08:16.490
Keep it in mind.

132
08:16.490 --> 08:17.420
Watch your step!

133
08:17.550 --> 08:18.880
Plant the markers deep!

134
08:19.470 --> 08:20.370
Watch your step!

135
08:20.370 --> 08:21.530
Plant the markers!

136
08:26.020 --> 08:27.380
Step on the grass roots!

137
08:27.440 --> 08:29.170
Stay out of the puddles!

138
08:29.290 --> 08:30.900
One after another!

139
08:32.870 --> 08:34.200
Step on the grass roots!

140
08:34.230 --> 08:35.950
Stay out of the puddles!

141
08:36.070 --> 08:37.190
Pass it down!

142
08:37.230 --> 08:38.380
Walk on the grass roots!

143
08:38.380 --> 08:39.590
Keep out of the water!

144
08:39.590 --> 08:40.020
Pass it down!

145
08:40.020 --> 08:41.070
Step on the grass roots!

146
08:41.070 --> 08:42.250
Stick to the grass roots!

147
08:42.250 --> 08:43.720
Avoid the puddles!

148
08:43.870 --> 08:45.110
Single file!

149
08:45.230 --> 08:46.190
Pass it down!

150
08:46.500 --> 08:47.830
Walk on the roots!

151
08:47.830 --> 08:49.230
Avoid the water!

152
08:49.230 --> 08:50.190
Pass it down!

153
08:50.990 --> 08:52.310
Step on the roots!

154
08:52.310 --> 08:53.540
Avoid the water!

155
08:53.540 --> 08:54.500
Pass it down!

156
09:17.740 --> 09:18.990
Years later,

157
09:19.700 --> 09:21.240
an American writer who traveled to China

158
09:21.240 --> 09:23.720
to chronicle the Long March

159
09:24.140 --> 09:26.350
described the scene in his book:

160
09:27.020 --> 09:29.140
this endless expanse of grassland

161
09:29.230 --> 09:31.960
was a magical carpet woven from vibrant flowers.

162
09:33.190 --> 09:36.540
But in the eyes of the Red Army soldiers,

163
09:37.140 --> 09:40.200
this magic carpet, though breathtakingly beautiful,

164
09:40.350 --> 09:43.530
was also terrifyingly vast and dead.

165
09:46.140 --> 09:47.270
Walking through it,

166
09:47.780 --> 09:49.870
they felt like they were plummeting

167
09:49.870 --> 09:52.200
into an infinite and colorful wasteland,

168
09:52.830 --> 09:55.630
their hearts gripped by the terror of the unknown.

169
09:58.440 --> 09:59.700
A medic from the 1st Red Army

170
09:59.700 --> 10:01.460
later recalled,

171
10:02.710 --> 10:04.170
we marched for days on end,

172
10:04.540 --> 10:07.470
and there wasn't a single soul for hundreds of miles.

173
10:07.710 --> 10:08.310
It felt like

174
10:08.310 --> 10:11.730
we were the very last people left on Earth.

175
10:23.050 --> 10:24.100
Comrades!

176
10:25.660 --> 10:27.190
Stick close to me!

177
10:27.420 --> 10:28.380
Remember!

178
10:28.660 --> 10:32.200
We only walk where the pathfinders planted their sticks!

179
10:33.020 --> 10:35.990
That's the lifeline they carved out for us!

180
10:36.010 --> 10:37.140
Step anywhere else,

181
10:38.210 --> 10:41.540
and you might just plunge straight into hell's boiling pot!

182
13:23.670 --> 13:26.620
[Huang Zhen, Chief of the Propaganda Section, Political Department of the Directly Subordinate Units, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

183
13:56.420 --> 13:57.950
Guo, when are we eating?

184
13:58.590 --> 13:59.500
I'm starving.

185
13:59.590 --> 14:01.190
You just ate this afternoon.

186
14:01.470 --> 14:02.730
Hungry again already?

187
14:02.750 --> 14:04.680
I have no idea what's wrong with me.

188
14:04.780 --> 14:06.780
My stomach's like a bottomless pit!

189
14:06.900 --> 14:09.100
I get hungry the second I finish eating!

190
14:14.620 --> 14:15.810
It's raining!

191
14:16.260 --> 14:18.030
[Peng Dehuai, Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

192
14:24.900 --> 14:25.590
Make camp.

193
14:25.660 --> 14:26.210
Take cover.

194
14:26.210 --> 14:26.810
Yes, sir!

195
14:26.990 --> 14:28.950
Halt and make camp!

196
14:28.990 --> 14:30.830
Take cover from the rain!

197
14:30.910 --> 14:32.180
Set up camp right here!

198
14:33.540 --> 14:34.780
We need to wait out the rain!

199
14:34.780 --> 14:35.950
Take cover!

200
14:36.480 --> 14:37.680
Pitch the tents!

201
14:39.380 --> 14:41.040
We're making camp right here!

202
14:43.920 --> 14:44.640
Hurry it up!

203
14:44.710 --> 14:46.070
Everyone, huddle under the wok!

204
14:46.070 --> 14:47.700
Alright, alright.

205
15:06.260 --> 15:07.260
Come on, alright.

206
15:17.940 --> 15:21.020
[Xiao Jinguang, Chief of Staff, 3rd Red Army Corps]

207
15:37.950 --> 15:39.990
Guo, squeeze in a bit.

208
15:40.070 --> 15:41.110
Don't catch a chill.

209
15:41.110 --> 15:41.830
I know.

210
15:42.070 --> 15:43.540
Don't let yourselves get drenched.

211
15:43.540 --> 15:45.540
You little guys...

212
15:45.740 --> 15:47.140
you're not built for this weather.

213
15:47.140 --> 15:49.860
One drop of rain and you'll fall sick.

214
16:17.740 --> 16:20.340
[Yang Shangkun, Political Commissar, 3rd Red Army Corps]

215
16:56.390 --> 16:59.060
Here's our current position.

216
17:03.620 --> 17:06.310
Comrade Jiaxiang, is he awake yet?

217
17:06.490 --> 17:08.040
No, he's still asleep.

218
17:09.240 --> 17:11.220
I managed to get some fresh water. Take a sip.

219
17:11.220 --> 17:13.550
I'm not thirsty. Give it to Comrade Enlai.

220
17:28.270 --> 17:29.200
Commander Peng!

221
17:29.260 --> 17:30.190
Commander Peng!

222
17:30.900 --> 17:33.210
I brought you some water. Have a drink.

223
17:38.980 --> 17:39.830
This rain

224
17:40.620 --> 17:42.020
comes fast and goes fast.

225
17:47.030 --> 17:48.030
Inform the troops.

226
17:48.030 --> 17:48.700
We keep moving.

227
17:48.700 --> 17:49.230
Yes, sir.

228
17:50.980 --> 17:51.870
Bugler!

229
17:51.940 --> 17:52.620
Here, sir!

230
17:52.790 --> 17:54.510
Sound the horn. We're marching out.

231
17:54.510 --> 17:55.220
Yes, sir!

232
18:03.870 --> 18:04.590
Move out!

233
18:04.590 --> 18:05.790
Let's go, let's go!

234
18:08.090 --> 18:08.600
We're moving out!

235
18:08.600 --> 18:09.670
Pack it up, boys!

236
18:15.540 --> 18:16.370
Jiaxiang.

237
18:17.140 --> 18:18.700
If you can't make it, get on the stretcher.

238
18:18.700 --> 18:19.570
I'm fine.

239
18:20.420 --> 18:21.550
I can walk.

240
18:21.680 --> 18:23.030
How's Comrade Enlai holding up?

241
18:23.030 --> 18:23.830
He's alright.

242
18:23.980 --> 18:25.240
He just had some water.

243
18:25.940 --> 18:26.980
We're moving out.

244
18:27.110 --> 18:28.770
Don't leave anything behind!

245
18:29.380 --> 18:31.180
Squad Leader, we're moving out!

246
18:31.590 --> 18:32.700
Squad Leader?

247
18:33.940 --> 18:35.090
Get your gear sorted, everyone!

248
18:35.090 --> 18:36.620
Squad Leader, time to go!

249
18:38.700 --> 18:39.140
Squad Leader?

250
18:39.140 --> 18:40.180
Get your gear sorted, everyone!

251
18:40.180 --> 18:40.790
Squad Leader!

252
18:40.790 --> 18:41.620
-Don't leave anything behind! -We're moving out!

253
18:41.620 --> 18:42.940
Comrade! Comrade!

254
18:42.960 --> 18:45.490
Comrade, what's wrong with our squad leader?

255
18:48.870 --> 18:52.550
Comrade... your squad leader is gone.

256
18:54.660 --> 18:55.790
That's impossible!

257
18:56.220 --> 18:58.020
He was perfectly fine just a minute ago!

258
18:58.020 --> 18:59.350
It's freezing out here.

259
18:59.380 --> 19:01.300
The march drained all his body heat.

260
19:01.300 --> 19:03.760
A sudden drop in temperature is fatal.

261
19:03.790 --> 19:04.900
Squad Leader!

262
19:05.700 --> 19:06.740
Squad Leader!

263
19:13.940 --> 19:15.150
Comrade.

264
19:16.070 --> 19:17.180
Time to go, comrade.

265
19:17.180 --> 19:18.180
Wake up!

266
19:19.250 --> 19:20.370
Let's go. Let's go.

267
19:29.110 --> 19:31.270
Squad Leader, you have to be okay!

268
19:31.310 --> 19:33.080
Squad Leader, you can't die!

269
19:33.110 --> 19:34.710
Squad Leader! Squad Leader!

270
19:34.750 --> 19:36.550
Squad Leader, please don't die!

271
19:36.900 --> 19:37.980
I'll save you, Squad Leader!

272
19:37.980 --> 19:38.690
Squad Leader!

273
19:38.690 --> 19:40.840
I'll save you!

274
19:41.030 --> 19:42.730
You can't leave us!

275
19:44.500 --> 19:47.670
Squad Leader! Squad Leader!

276
19:48.440 --> 19:50.040
Comrade, stop crying.

277
19:50.180 --> 19:51.670
Squad Leader!

278
19:54.350 --> 19:55.310
Little comrade!

279
19:55.980 --> 19:57.110
Little comrade!

280
19:57.510 --> 19:58.350
How is he?

281
19:58.490 --> 20:00.020
He's fine, just passed out.

282
20:00.270 --> 20:01.660
Guards, bring Dahei over here!

283
20:01.660 --> 20:01.980
Yes, sir!

284
20:01.980 --> 20:03.110
Come on, help him up.

285
20:06.180 --> 20:06.850
Easy now.

286
20:08.420 --> 20:09.350
Hold him steady.

287
20:54.420 --> 20:55.330
Move out!

288
22:22.620 --> 22:23.590
Are you alright?

289
22:32.510 --> 22:33.510
Before we set out,

290
22:34.240 --> 22:37.100
I sent a telegram to Zhang Guotao.

291
22:37.120 --> 22:39.360
And I still haven't gotten a reply.

292
22:40.840 --> 22:43.600
Chen Changhao and Xu Xiangqian

293
22:44.510 --> 22:45.980
also sent him telegrams

294
22:46.380 --> 22:48.380
in their own names,

295
22:49.070 --> 22:50.180
telling him

296
22:50.980 --> 22:53.980
that there's no turning back, and we must advance.

297
22:55.060 --> 22:56.060
But...

298
22:57.140 --> 22:59.090
they never heard back either.

299
22:59.750 --> 23:05.160
We don't have any other choice right now.

300
23:07.310 --> 23:12.520
We just have to make it out of these endless marshlands first,

301
23:13.940 --> 23:17.160
and figure it out from there.

302
23:18.660 --> 23:19.380
Comrade!

303
23:21.070 --> 23:21.830
Comrade!

304
24:22.880 --> 24:23.680
Chairman!

305
24:41.800 --> 24:43.000
Over here, come on.

306
25:22.730 --> 25:23.810
We can eat this.

307
25:23.840 --> 25:24.760
Here.

308
26:41.130 --> 26:43.460
Mind the wound. Don't let it get infected.

309
26:46.180 --> 26:47.010
Chen Geng.

310
26:48.180 --> 26:49.770
Have Vice Chairman Zhou and Comrade Wang eaten yet?

311
26:49.770 --> 26:51.760
I'm dishing it out for them right now.

312
26:51.760 --> 26:53.560
What are they having? Let me see.

313
26:58.620 --> 27:00.620
They're incredibly weak right now.

314
27:00.790 --> 27:02.920
This watery broth has zero nutrition.

315
27:03.550 --> 27:05.080
Got any roasted flour left?

316
27:07.420 --> 27:07.980
Here.

317
27:08.460 --> 27:09.220
Li.

318
27:37.750 --> 27:38.880
I'm completely out.

319
27:39.420 --> 27:40.820
Even if I had just a pinch,

320
27:40.980 --> 27:42.980
it wouldn't be this thin and watery.

321
27:45.420 --> 27:47.540
Here, take this to them.

322
27:47.570 --> 27:48.100
Yes, sir.

323
27:48.110 --> 27:48.750
Go on.

324
27:48.770 --> 27:49.560
Here.

325
27:50.980 --> 27:51.710
There you go.

326
27:51.870 --> 27:53.270
Careful, don't spill it!

327
27:59.210 --> 28:01.630
Here, comrade, have some water.

328
28:26.040 --> 28:26.550
Thank you.

329
28:26.550 --> 28:27.220
Thanks.

330
28:31.830 --> 28:32.490
Here you go.

331
28:32.620 --> 28:33.830
Mr. Dong! Mr. Dong!

332
28:33.830 --> 28:35.460
Mr. Lin! Mr. Dong!

333
28:35.460 --> 28:36.460
Drink some water.

334
28:36.700 --> 28:38.560
Everyone, have some water first.

335
28:38.700 --> 28:39.510
Here.

336
28:39.790 --> 28:41.310
I'll just set these greens down here.

337
28:41.310 --> 28:41.840
Alright.

338
28:42.030 --> 28:42.980
Is that enough for you?

339
28:42.980 --> 28:43.790
Yes.

340
28:43.830 --> 28:44.310
Great.

341
28:44.330 --> 28:46.530
Let me see what's brewing in here.

342
28:47.830 --> 28:49.180
Here, add some water.

343
28:49.420 --> 28:51.430
You ladies,

344
28:52.030 --> 28:54.270
how are you planning to do with

345
28:54.270 --> 28:55.620
this leather boot?

346
28:57.940 --> 28:59.730
We've boiled it.

347
29:00.030 --> 29:00.900
We've roasted it.

348
29:00.900 --> 29:02.590
We're trying a whole new recipe.

349
29:02.590 --> 29:03.850
Eating it in sections!

350
29:04.340 --> 29:05.800
In sections! In sections!

351
29:06.070 --> 29:06.700
Look here.

352
29:06.750 --> 29:08.040
This part

353
29:08.090 --> 29:10.760
[He Zizhen, Wife of Mao Zedong]

354
29:08.240 --> 29:09.800
is the softest and thinnest part.

355
29:09.800 --> 29:10.870
You just need to take it to the fire,

356
29:10.870 --> 29:12.310
singe off the fur on the outside,

357
29:12.310 --> 29:14.070
then scrape off the charred layer

358
29:14.070 --> 29:15.180
and it's ready to boil!

359
29:15.180 --> 29:17.350
It tastes perfectly crisp.

360
29:17.700 --> 29:19.100
Now, this middle section

361
29:19.230 --> 29:20.310
is just like a leather belt.

362
29:20.310 --> 29:21.070
Just boil it

363
29:21.140 --> 29:22.430
like you would a leather belt.

364
29:22.430 --> 29:23.460
Roast it over the fire

365
29:23.460 --> 29:25.380
until it puffs up and gets crispy,

366
29:25.440 --> 29:27.270
then toss it in the pot to boil.

367
29:27.550 --> 29:29.980
But this thick upper and the sole?

368
29:30.140 --> 29:32.180
They're heavy and smell awful.

369
29:32.340 --> 29:33.860
So they need special treatment.

370
29:33.860 --> 29:37.670
First, we scorch the whole piece of leather,

371
29:37.830 --> 29:40.030
then scrape that layer off entirely.

372
29:40.140 --> 29:42.070
Throw it in water. It needs to soak.

373
29:42.070 --> 29:43.750
You have to soak it for a really long time.

374
29:43.750 --> 29:45.460
Then it goes into the pot.

375
29:45.660 --> 29:48.180
Once the leather turns soft and chewy,

376
29:48.350 --> 29:49.210
it's good to go!

377
29:49.280 --> 29:52.140
[Dong Biwu, Secretary of the General Party Branch of the Cadre Convalescence Company]

378
29:49.750 --> 29:51.140
Look at this toe cap!

379
29:51.290 --> 29:52.380
It might look like the toughest part,

380
29:52.380 --> 29:53.610
but if you prep it right,

381
29:53.610 --> 29:55.470
out of the whole thing, it becomes

382
29:55.550 --> 29:57.230
the most tender and chewy part!

383
29:57.230 --> 29:58.420
The flavor is absolutely divine!

384
29:58.420 --> 30:00.080
We almost can't bear to eat it.

385
30:01.140 --> 30:03.030
You ladies really know how to eat.

386
30:03.460 --> 30:04.620
You've turned it into a culinary art!

387
30:04.620 --> 30:06.620
This kind of experience is worth spreading!

388
30:06.620 --> 30:07.770
For these past couple of days,

389
30:07.770 --> 30:09.310
we've been surviving on nothing but wild greens and roots.

390
30:09.310 --> 30:10.220
So when Comrade Liu Ying,

391
30:10.220 --> 30:12.270
finally managed to bring us a leather boot,

392
30:12.270 --> 30:13.810
[Cai Chang, Wife of Li Fuchun]

393
30:12.390 --> 30:14.180
you bet we're going to savor every single bite!

394
30:14.180 --> 30:15.270
Exactly!

395
30:15.870 --> 30:17.270
As for the taste,

396
30:17.290 --> 30:18.210
I wouldn't bet my life on it.

397
30:18.210 --> 30:21.840
[Lin Boqu, Head of the General Supply Department of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

398
30:18.270 --> 30:20.790
But as long as there is life,

399
30:20.980 --> 30:22.500
the revolution will bloom!

400
30:22.500 --> 30:23.590
Well said!

401
30:23.620 --> 30:24.590
Well said!

402
30:24.980 --> 30:25.980
Mr. Dong! Mr. Lin!

403
30:26.110 --> 30:26.980
Come over and try our cooking

404
30:26.980 --> 30:28.310
once it's done.

405
30:28.520 --> 30:28.940
Sounds good!

406
30:28.940 --> 30:30.110
Great, great!

407
30:30.270 --> 30:32.380
We should really spread the word

408
30:32.480 --> 30:34.030
about this new way to cook boots!

409
30:34.030 --> 30:34.880
Right, exactly! Let's go!

410
30:34.880 --> 30:37.080
Comrades! Listen up! The leather boot

411
30:37.110 --> 30:38.790
can be cooked in a brand new way!

412
30:38.790 --> 30:40.060
That's right! A new recipe!

413
30:40.060 --> 30:41.310
Four different ways, actually!

414
30:41.310 --> 30:43.640
I'm just showing off what I just picked up!

415
30:43.910 --> 30:45.110
Let me help you portion out the wild herbs.

416
30:45.110 --> 30:46.510
Sure, sure! Sounds good!

417
30:47.320 --> 30:48.340
Mr. Lin! Hurry, grab a seat!

418
30:48.340 --> 30:49.000
Alright, alright!

419
30:49.000 --> 30:50.700
Everyone sit down! Have a seat!

420
30:50.700 --> 30:53.380
The rations we brought were already running low

421
30:53.550 --> 30:55.180
and we've been burning through them lately.

422
30:55.180 --> 30:58.070
A bunch of companies have completely run out of food.

423
30:58.070 --> 31:00.940
Over the last few days, between the exhaustion and the freezing cold,

424
31:00.940 --> 31:04.180
we've been losing more and more of our men.

425
31:04.980 --> 31:07.780
Just today, the stretcher unit alone lost six men!

426
31:08.830 --> 31:10.380
One comrade drops dead,

427
31:10.400 --> 31:12.700
another steps right up to take his place at the stretcher

428
31:12.700 --> 31:16.000
and barely takes a few steps before he's gone too.

429
31:18.810 --> 31:20.140
We can't go on like this.

430
31:20.310 --> 31:22.940
We need to pull together a squad of young and strong guys

431
31:22.940 --> 31:25.000
and form a dedicated stretcher unit.

432
31:27.750 --> 31:28.710
Commanders,

433
31:29.490 --> 31:32.490
could I be the captain of this new unit?

434
31:32.660 --> 31:34.080
I'm volunteering.

435
31:34.460 --> 31:35.220
Chen Geng,

436
31:35.270 --> 31:36.670
this is no time for jokes.

437
31:37.270 --> 31:38.200
Look at your leg!

438
31:38.200 --> 31:39.130
Sure,

439
31:39.310 --> 31:40.790
I can't carry a stretcher,

440
31:40.980 --> 31:42.790
but I know how to organize people!

441
31:42.790 --> 31:44.610
I can keep their spirits up!

442
31:49.130 --> 31:50.970
Being stuck with a leg like this

443
31:50.990 --> 31:52.220
has practically made me a doctor!

444
31:52.220 --> 31:54.820
I know exactly how to handle this kind of thing!

445
32:02.780 --> 32:03.740
Peng,

446
32:04.750 --> 32:07.480
I'm just sitting around doing nothing right now.

447
32:08.550 --> 32:11.280
Joining the stretcher unit is the best fit for me.

448
32:16.090 --> 32:17.570
Well then...

449
32:23.460 --> 32:24.390
the job is yours.

450
32:26.830 --> 32:27.790
Thank you, Commander!

451
32:27.790 --> 32:29.320
I swear I won't let you down!

452
32:31.660 --> 32:32.590
Comrades!

453
32:32.750 --> 32:34.350
We are officially forming a stretcher unit!

454
32:34.350 --> 32:35.820
Whoever wants in,

455
32:36.590 --> 32:37.440
raise your hand!

456
32:37.440 --> 32:38.180
I'm in!

457
32:38.210 --> 32:39.590
Me too!

458
32:39.620 --> 32:41.180
Put me down! Me too!

459
32:41.200 --> 32:43.200
I'm volunteering! Me too!

460
32:43.150 --> 32:45.940
[Yang Lisan, Director of the General Depot Department of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

461
32:43.980 --> 32:45.140
Comrade Lisan!

462
32:45.820 --> 32:47.270
With a build like yours,

463
32:47.620 --> 32:50.680
you'd make the perfect Captain for the stretcher unit!

464
32:51.380 --> 32:52.600
But you're a little late.

465
32:52.600 --> 32:55.360
The position has already been filled.

466
32:57.310 --> 32:58.370
Comrade Chen Geng,

467
32:58.420 --> 32:59.870
I don't care about titles.

468
32:59.870 --> 33:00.720
I've got the muscle.

469
33:00.720 --> 33:02.120
And it's not just muscle.

470
33:02.380 --> 33:03.540
I've got the grit to back it up!

471
33:03.540 --> 33:04.380
Good!

472
33:04.550 --> 33:07.140
Then you can be the Vice Captain!

473
33:07.270 --> 33:07.920
Deal!

474
33:09.050 --> 33:11.040
So it's official: the stretcher unit is established!

475
33:11.040 --> 33:11.720
Commander.

476
33:13.250 --> 33:13.980
How did it go?

477
33:14.110 --> 33:15.180
Vice Chairman Zhou and Director Wang

478
33:15.180 --> 33:16.620
only drank the wild herb soup.

479
33:16.620 --> 33:17.590
They said,

480
33:18.830 --> 33:22.090
"Save the roasted flour for the comrades who need it more."

481
33:28.220 --> 33:29.140
Chen Geng!

482
33:30.550 --> 33:31.460
You eat this!

483
33:32.110 --> 33:32.660
Me?

484
33:52.870 --> 33:53.750
Comrade Lisan!

485
33:53.980 --> 33:54.620
Yes sir!

486
33:55.510 --> 33:56.460
You eat this!

487
34:00.350 --> 34:01.480
I'm not eating that.

488
34:02.830 --> 34:03.760
That's an order!

489
34:04.550 --> 34:07.510
This is Order No. 1 for Chen Geng,

490
34:07.590 --> 34:09.830
Commander of the Stretcher Detachment,

491
34:09.830 --> 34:11.630
3rd Army of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army!

492
34:11.630 --> 34:12.170
Take it!

493
34:12.580 --> 34:14.239
Well, I'm still not eating it!

494
34:14.580 --> 34:15.380
Get back here!

495
34:16.310 --> 34:17.969
The stretcher unit has to eat!

496
34:18.540 --> 34:21.070
You can't carry anything on an empty stomach!

497
34:22.830 --> 34:24.230
I'll take the first bite!

498
34:38.310 --> 34:38.989
Eat!

499
34:46.449 --> 34:48.489
Comrades! Finish it all!

500
34:48.570 --> 34:49.360
Yes sir!

501
35:31.230 --> 35:32.900
Dinner is ready. Come and get it, everyone.

502
35:32.900 --> 35:34.310
Okay.

503
35:34.730 --> 35:35.930
Time to eat!

504
35:36.670 --> 35:37.940
Chopsticks are here!

505
35:45.150 --> 35:46.350
Here you go, Liu Ying.

506
35:47.060 --> 35:47.870
Grab a bowl.

507
35:59.710 --> 36:00.500
I'll get it.

508
36:04.980 --> 36:07.750
Eat the skin first, then drink the broth.

509
36:07.850 --> 36:11.060
As the saying goes, the broth of the food helps digest the food!

510
36:11.060 --> 36:12.380
These strips

511
36:12.420 --> 36:13.670
are a little undercooked.

512
36:13.670 --> 36:14.800
Kinda tough to chew.

513
36:14.900 --> 36:15.870
Well, nothing we can do about that.

514
36:15.870 --> 36:17.540
We're at a pretty high altitude up here.

515
36:17.540 --> 36:18.540
The water never quite reaches a full boil.

516
36:18.540 --> 36:19.900
No matter how long you boil it, it stays tough.

517
36:19.900 --> 36:22.020
Well, there's a bright side to it being tough!

518
36:22.020 --> 36:24.540
It takes longer to digest, so you don't get hungry as fast!

519
36:24.540 --> 36:26.630
What was that saying Mr. Lin just mentioned?

520
36:26.630 --> 36:29.100
"As long as there is life,

521
36:29.100 --> 36:31.350
the revolution will blossom!"

522
36:36.150 --> 36:37.090
A shooting star!

523
36:49.630 --> 36:50.670
So beautiful.

524
36:51.580 --> 36:53.100
Back when we were at Jinggang Mountain,

525
36:53.100 --> 36:54.830
I used to stargaze all the time.

526
36:54.870 --> 36:57.020
I thought Jinggang Mountain was so high up,

527
36:57.020 --> 36:58.750
that I was seeing a ton of stars.

528
36:58.910 --> 36:59.900
But I have never seen

529
36:59.900 --> 37:01.830
as many stars as there are tonight.

530
37:03.350 --> 37:04.610
This Milky Way

531
37:05.230 --> 37:06.340
truly looks like a vast river,

532
37:06.340 --> 37:08.340
rushing right through the heavens.

533
37:09.110 --> 37:11.310
You can almost see every single splash.

534
37:11.670 --> 37:14.540
How many stars are there in this Milky Way?

535
37:14.980 --> 37:16.310
Too many to count.

536
37:16.710 --> 37:19.460
I wonder what they're all named.

537
37:20.230 --> 37:23.060
Look at those seven stars lined up right there.

538
37:23.060 --> 37:24.660
The ones shaped like a spoon.

539
37:24.870 --> 37:26.380
That's the Big Dipper.

540
37:26.460 --> 37:28.190
That's the easiest one to spot.

541
37:28.380 --> 37:29.640
You're totally right!

542
37:29.790 --> 37:31.750
See that brightest one right next to the heavenly river?

543
37:31.750 --> 37:32.390
You see it?

544
37:32.670 --> 37:34.530
That's Altair, the Cowherd star.

545
37:34.870 --> 37:37.150
Those two little stars beside it

546
37:37.190 --> 37:39.380
are like a carrying pole balancing his two children.

547
37:39.380 --> 37:41.230
What about Vega, the Weaver Girl star?

548
37:41.230 --> 37:43.750
The one across the heavenly river is Vega.

549
38:22.390 --> 38:30.070
Little stars, little stars, fill the sky.

550
38:31.680 --> 38:38.890
Fly to the west bank of Yongxin River.

551
38:40.110 --> 38:43.120
One to the east.

552
38:43.870 --> 38:47.030
One to the west.

553
38:47.560 --> 38:54.760
Count and count, there's no end in sight.

554
38:55.350 --> 39:03.790
Mama calls me for dinner.

555
39:03.790 --> 39:11.870
And I want to count the stars above.

556
39:11.890 --> 39:19.760
Each one twinkling so bright.

557
39:20.740 --> 39:28.450
Twinkling, twinkling, blinking at me.

558
39:30.190 --> 39:39.050
One star, two stars.

559
39:40.670 --> 39:48.870
Starlight guiding the way, I'm brave enough to walk.

560
39:50.420 --> 39:58.980
Walk till dawn, when the rooster crows.

561
40:00.130 --> 40:09.280
Little stars hide and play peekaboo with me.

562
40:09.800 --> 40:20.370
Little stars hide and play peekaboo with me.

563
40:21.210 --> 40:21.920
That was lovely! Great!

564
40:21.920 --> 40:22.960
So beautiful!

565
40:24.150 --> 40:25.190
Sounds amazing!

566
40:25.270 --> 40:26.980
Bravo, bravo!

567
40:28.410 --> 40:30.330
Excellent, excellent!

568
40:33.580 --> 40:37.460
Mother, shall I tell you?

569
40:37.460 --> 40:38.710
Stand up, stand up!

570
40:38.710 --> 40:39.710
Get in the middle!

571
40:39.830 --> 40:40.490
Go on, go on!

572
40:40.790 --> 40:46.020
What is it that torments me?

573
40:47.350 --> 40:51.630
Ever since I laid eyes on the fairy Sylvandre,

574
40:51.710 --> 40:57.060
with her gentle eyes gazing upon me,

575
40:57.830 --> 41:03.190
my heart speaks in every moment:

576
41:03.940 --> 41:09.790
"How can one live without love?"

577
41:10.100 --> 41:10.940
Bravo!

578
41:11.060 --> 41:13.980
Amazing! Beautiful!

579
41:14.540 --> 41:16.900
Sounds fantastic!

580
41:53.160 --> 41:53.950
Guo.

581
41:55.420 --> 41:56.870
I've let you guys down.

582
41:57.310 --> 41:58.350
This is all we have.

583
41:58.350 --> 41:58.980
Guo,

584
41:59.120 --> 42:00.510
nobody is blaming you.

585
42:00.660 --> 42:02.350
Anything hot will do.

586
42:08.310 --> 42:11.150
How about I whip up a dish for everyone?

587
42:11.150 --> 42:11.730
Sounds great!

588
42:11.730 --> 42:12.560
Yeah, yeah!

589
42:12.590 --> 42:13.190
Come on!

590
42:13.790 --> 42:15.460
What are you cooking this time?

591
42:15.460 --> 42:19.820
How about stir-fried smoked bamboo shoots with pork, Jinggang Mountain style?

592
42:19.820 --> 42:20.190
Sounds perfect!

593
42:20.190 --> 42:20.840
Great!

594
42:20.980 --> 42:21.940
Now, for this dish,

595
42:21.940 --> 42:23.380
you have to use

596
42:23.670 --> 42:27.150
the local smoked bamboo shoots from Jinggang Mountain,

597
42:27.380 --> 42:30.100
along with pork belly and some chili peppers.

598
42:30.310 --> 42:31.760
When you're stir-frying it,

599
42:31.760 --> 42:33.850
first, you take these smoked bamboo shoots

600
42:33.850 --> 42:35.120
and sauté them up a bit,

601
42:35.270 --> 42:36.750
just to cook all the moisture out.

602
42:36.750 --> 42:38.460
That's the only way the oil really seeps in.

603
42:38.460 --> 42:39.100
Oh, right,

604
42:39.230 --> 42:40.690
when you're making it, don't forget

605
42:40.690 --> 42:42.690
you gotta sneak in a little vinegar.

606
42:42.790 --> 42:43.460
Guo,

607
42:43.630 --> 42:44.630
we add the soy sauce and vinegar

608
42:44.630 --> 42:45.940
right out in the open.

609
42:45.940 --> 42:47.600
Why do you call it "sneaking"?

610
42:47.980 --> 42:48.500
Yeah, exactly!

611
42:48.500 --> 42:49.980
See, you guys just don't get it.

612
42:49.980 --> 42:52.460
This is a secret trick

613
42:52.830 --> 42:55.030
that only the veteran chefs know about.

614
42:55.190 --> 42:57.230
"Sneaking" the vinegar means

615
42:57.350 --> 42:59.190
you can't go overboard.

616
42:59.310 --> 43:01.980
You want to bring out its rich and savory flavor,

617
43:02.190 --> 43:03.750
but without actually making it sour!
